From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 10:06:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Hoist the constant block states out of the generation loops

setBlocksInChunk re-resolved Blocks.STONE.getBlockData() and the ocean
block on every one of the 65536 iterations of its innermost loop, and
read settings.seaLevel there too. generateBiomeTerrain did the same for
bedrock and stone across a 256-step column scan that runs once per
column, so also 65536 times per chunk.

Measured over 625 chunks generated from a fixed seed: 6.578s -> 6.365s,
about 3%.

That is roughly the ceiling for this method without changing what it
produces. generateBiomeTerrain calls random.nextInt(5) once per y per
column - 65536 draws per chunk - and the number of draws determines
every terrain feature downstream, so no iteration of that loop can be
skipped. The noise generation has the same property through floating
point operation order.

The 625-chunk comparison confirms every stored field is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BiomeBase.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BiomeBase.java
